  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (12 of 12). I haven't made a commit.\n\nThe new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They cover each part of the spec, including the exact examples from its tables:\n- version syntax and invalid input, which returns `false` without throwing\n- prerelease and build ordering\n- comparators, `||` sets, wildcards and partial versions\n- tilde, caret and hyphen ranges\n- the rule that a prerelease version only matches when a comparator in the same set has a prerelease on the same `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`\n\nWhere the spec is silent I made these choices:\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing. `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- **`~ 1` and `^ 1`:** a space after `~` or `^` makes the range invalid, because the spec only allows a space after `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` and `=`.\n- **Wildcards:** a wildcard in one position makes every later position a wildcard, so `1.x.3` means `1.x`.\n- **Partial versions:** a prerelease or build suffix on a partial version, such as `1.x-beta`, is invalid.\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** numeric ones may have leading zeros, since the spec only forbids leading zeros in major, minor and patch.",
